{"id":"u-aacc57b9-bc38-40fe-8252-82aaba43a493","src":"community","title":"Valkyrie 5.0 - Women Ultimate Training Program","author":"Tuomas S.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ftl0pt-valkyrie-50-women-ultimate-training-program","desc":"🔱 THE PURPOSE OF THE CHRONICLE\nThis is not just another training split—this is a 3-day full-body odyssey forged for the modern Valkyrie. In Norse lore, the Valkyries were fierce, beautiful, and unmatched shieldmaidens who chose who would rise to glory. The purpose of this program is to build a physique worthy of those legends.\n\nWe focus heavily on the hinterlands (the glutes), utilizing movements like the Squat, Hip Thrust, and Smith Machine Step-Ups to build an iron foundation, a sovereign lower body, and unparalleled strength. Combined with strategic upper-body strikes to carve out a commanding \"hourglass\" posture, this saga transforms a novice lifter into an unstoppable force. You will build mass where it matters, command the iron, and claim your throne.\n\n🛡️ RULES OF THE BATTLEGROUND\nBefore you lift the steel, you must understand the laws of the forge:\n\n1. The Pre-Battle Ritual (Warm-Ups)\nNever enter a raid cold. For your heavy compound sagas (like Squats or Bench Press), you must perform at least 2–3 warm-up sets before your official working sets.\n\n⚡ Valkyrie’s Secret: You do not need to rest between your warm-up sets. Keep the blood flowing, build the mind-muscle connection, and save your true rest for the real war.\n\n2. The Shield-Wall Rest (Rest Periods)\nWhen you strike with true intensity (@8 to @10 RPE), your muscles will scream. To maintain your power and conquer the next set, you must rest for 2–3 minutes between working sets. Do not rush. A tired warrior fails the lift; a rested Valkyrie shatters records.\n\nLet the drums of war beat. Enter the gym, claim your gains, and let Valhalla hear your triumph!","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":13,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-26T16:04:23.766Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Full Body /Glute & Squat Heavy","Full Body / Back & Booty Sculp","Full Body / Hourglass & Glute"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"r":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Preacher Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Abs crunch w/ ropes","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Step Ups (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Leg Press)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dumbell Overhead Press (Sitting)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9},{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Glute Kickback (Cable)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hyperextension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"r":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"rp